# =====================================================================
# Release V075 -- Scheduling pkg (2-4/n): Chair Utilisation model
# =====================================================================
# Splits the old single "chair_utilisation" (scheduled/worked) into three metrics:
#   diary_fill                  = scheduled appt hours / worked hours (how full the diary is;
#                                 the only one computable forwards; can exceed 100%)
#   chair_utilisation           = ACTUAL capped in-chair hours / worked hours (real time in the
#                                 chair; capped at next appt start or diary end-of-day so unclosed
#                                 sessions can't overstate it; untracked appts fall back to duration)
#   patient_tracked_in_surgery  = appts with an in-surgery timestamp / all appts (reception tracking)
#
#   * Aggregate gains Chair_Hours + Tracked_Appointments (capped-chair logic, LEAD to next appt).
#   * Fact_Metric_Actuals renames the old chair_utilisation rows -> diary_fill and adds the two new
#     metrics (tenant + practitioner grain).
#   * Config.Metric_Definitions: chair_utilisation redefined (actual), diary_fill + patient_tracked
#     added. All three carry targets (appear in the targets spreadsheet).
#
# Deploy AFTER V074 (diary Is_Dummy + synthetic entries). Order below matters: the aggregate TABLE
# must carry the new columns before the metric-actuals SP is (re)created (Fabric validates eagerly).
# Rebuild data via Orchestrate_Build, then re-apply the Tabular Editor scheduling script + refresh.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V075__scheduling_chair_util_metrics.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.Aggregate_Site_Patient_Practitioner_Daily.Table.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Site_Patient_Practitioner_Daily.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Metric_Actuals.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Metric_Definitions.Data.sql

TEST
